    <body>
        <segment id="1" parent="11" relname="preparation">Good point P41.</segment>
        <segment id="2" parent="12" relname="span">I agree with what you have said here.</segment>
        <segment id="3" parent="13" relname="span">Especially the part about intuitiveness depending on the user's familiarity and previous experiences.</segment>
        <segment id="4" parent="17" relname="span">Experts can find many things that are not intuitive to them,</segment>
        <segment id="5" parent="4" relname="nonvolitional-cause">because they have used the technology over and over again.</segment>
        <segment id="6" parent="17" relname="elaboration">Based on their experience, many things seem very natural to them,</segment>
        <segment id="7" parent="16" relname="elaboration">and very little effort is exerted with respect to learning how to do things.</segment>
        <segment id="8" parent="14" relname="span">But a novice will almost always recognize whether something is intuitive or not.</segment>
        <segment id="9" parent="12" relname="evaluation">Very interesting idea to discuss.</segment>
        <group id="10" type="span"/>
        <group id="11" type="span" parent="10" relname="span"/>
        <group id="12" type="span" parent="11" relname="span"/>
        <group id="13" type="span" parent="2" relname="elaboration"/>
        <group id="14" type="span" parent="3" relname="elaboration"/>
        <group id="15" type="span" parent="8" relname="antithesis"/>
        <group id="16" type="span" parent="15" relname="span"/>
        <group id="17" type="span" parent="16" relname="span"/>
    </body>
